WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.837 --> 00:00:09.837
Don't shout at me.

00:00:09.879 --> 00:00:11.087
So can please tell me?

00:00:11.587 --> 00:00:12.420
I'm not going to.

00:00:13.962 --> 00:00:15.004
Please wait.

00:00:16.879 --> 00:00:18.712
You know, I've covered a lot of companies.

00:00:18.712 --> 00:00:21.962
I've covered a lot of
Machiavellian companies

00:00:21.962 --> 00:00:24.087
where, you know, people play rough.

00:00:24.087 --> 00:00:26.004
I don't think I've ever seen anything

00:00:26.004 --> 00:00:27.795
on the scale of Nissan.

00:00:27.795 --> 00:00:30.504
- He is making you, but you act for Nissan.

00:00:30.504 --> 00:00:32.045
I mean, it's corrupt.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:35.337
One of the most dramatic elements

00:00:35.337 --> 00:00:39.295
was Ravinder Passi's home being raided

00:00:39.295 --> 00:00:42.129
by court officials in Yokohama.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:45.045
- You scared my wife,
you scared my children.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.129
I worked at Nissan for 16 years.

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:51.754
So Rav Passi's journey
into the darkest recesses

00:00:51.754 --> 00:00:53.795
of the Japanese corporate world

00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:56.420
started when he was the general counsel,

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.962
the highest corporate lawyer
position in the company.

00:00:59.962 --> 00:01:02.670
- [Reporter] In the past few minutes,
Nissan has revealed

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:05.379
that its chairman has been arrested

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:08.920
after allegations of serious misconduct.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.462
He was tasked with
investigating Carlos Ghosn.

00:01:14.004 --> 00:01:18.337
And he was told, conduct
an internal investigation

00:01:18.337 --> 00:01:20.212
and get to the heart of the matter.

00:01:21.754 --> 00:01:24.170
And then along the way
he started to notice

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:26.129
serious conflicts of interest.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.254
He is one of the few people who knows

00:01:32.254 --> 00:01:34.545
an extreme amount of detail

00:01:34.545 --> 00:01:38.462
regarding the alleged
crimes by Carlos Ghosn.

00:01:38.462 --> 00:01:42.379
And he's now ready to tell
his own story on the record

00:01:42.379 --> 00:01:44.545
about some of the events that happened.

00:01:59.045 --> 00:02:00.629
My name's Ravinder Passi.

00:02:00.629 --> 00:02:03.670
I'm the former global general counsel

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.670
of Nissan Motor Co. Limited.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:09.504
And you could say yes,
I had a front row seat

00:02:09.504 --> 00:02:11.129
in terms of what was going on.

00:02:12.337 --> 00:02:15.504
- [Reporter] When Carlos Ghosn saved Nissan years ago

00:02:15.504 --> 00:02:18.295
he was depicted in Japanese
comic books as this hero.

00:02:18.295 --> 00:02:22.337
And now maybe we'll see comic
books where he's the villain.

00:02:22.337 --> 00:02:26.379
In corporate Japan, Nissan
was quite an unusual company.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:31.379
It was led for two decades
by a non-Japanese executive.

00:02:33.337 --> 00:02:35.420
Well, Carlos Ghosn was a hero

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.254
in the Japanese business world.

00:02:37.254 --> 00:02:39.962
If you had a global business celebrity

00:02:39.962 --> 00:02:44.420
in Japan and worldwide, it
was definitely Carlos Ghosn.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.087
- [Reporter] In a country with few foreigners

00:02:46.087 --> 00:02:48.504
at the top, he stood out.

00:02:48.504 --> 00:02:51.629
But over the years he saved
Nissan from bankruptcy,

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:53.712
allied with Renault and Mitsubishi,

00:02:53.712 --> 00:02:55.379
and turn the alliance into one

00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:57.879
of the most competitive in the world.

00:02:57.879 --> 00:02:59.879
Yet as the years went on,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.170
I think his ambitions
changed a little bit.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.379
He started thinking about legacy plays.

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:07.462
And one of them was to
really tighten the alliance

00:03:07.462 --> 00:03:11.129
between Renault and Japan.

00:03:11.129 --> 00:03:14.712
And unbeknownst to him,
there was a contingent

00:03:14.712 --> 00:03:17.045
of senior Nissan executives

00:03:17.045 --> 00:03:21.212
that were really felt
threatened by that move.

00:03:21.212 --> 00:03:22.462
They really thought that they would

00:03:22.462 --> 00:03:26.379
lose complete control of the car company.

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:27.712
And even in the government

00:03:27.712 --> 00:03:30.295
there was probably a little bit of anxiety

00:03:30.295 --> 00:03:34.337
about a national champion
in the auto industry

00:03:34.337 --> 00:03:37.837
falling under full-blown foreign control.

00:03:37.837 --> 00:03:40.712
- [Reporter] Carlos Ghosn was an auto industry leader

00:03:40.712 --> 00:03:43.337
respected by many in Japan.

00:03:43.337 --> 00:03:45.129
Now he's in jail.

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:46.587
The arrest of Carlos Ghosn

00:03:46.587 --> 00:03:48.920
came completely out of the blue.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.129
This was in November of 2018.

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:54.379
He was coming to Japan
on Nissan's corporate jet

00:03:54.379 --> 00:03:57.545
for a regular executive meeting.

00:03:57.545 --> 00:04:01.462
And he was met on the tarmac
by Japanese authorities

00:04:01.462 --> 00:04:04.670
who whisked him away to jail

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:08.504
and charged him with
financial misconduct crimes.

00:04:08.504 --> 00:04:10.129
So what happened was that

00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:13.754
a power struggle ensued inside the company

00:04:13.754 --> 00:04:17.462
and somewhere along the
way it was criminalized.

00:04:17.462 --> 00:04:21.337
By that I mean that there were allegations

00:04:21.337 --> 00:04:24.295
leveled at Carlos Ghosn about the way

00:04:24.295 --> 00:04:27.587
he reported his pay to
Japanese authorities,

00:04:27.587 --> 00:04:30.879
the way he handled money
inside the company,

00:04:30.879 --> 00:04:34.254
that in other contexts
might've been a board action,

00:04:34.254 --> 00:04:37.045
might've been handled internally.

00:04:37.045 --> 00:04:39.254
A number of executives at Nissan decided

00:04:39.254 --> 00:04:42.212
to take this difference

00:04:42.212 --> 00:04:45.420
and take it over to the
Tokyo Prosecutor's Office.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:48.170
And that unleashed a chain of events

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:50.254
that would shake the entire auto industry.

00:04:54.795 --> 00:04:57.462
So after Carlos Ghosn was arrested,

00:04:57.462 --> 00:05:00.379
Nissan launched an internal investigation

00:05:00.379 --> 00:05:04.004
into the events that led up to his arrest.

00:05:04.004 --> 00:05:09.004
So Rav Passi is tasked with
investigating Carlos Ghosn.

00:05:09.087 --> 00:05:11.504
And he was told, get to
the heart of the matter.

00:05:11.504 --> 00:05:14.295
Find out what Carlos Ghosn did wrong

00:05:14.295 --> 00:05:17.712
and bring it to our shareholders.

00:05:17.712 --> 00:05:19.587
Yeah, it's really complicated

00:05:19.587 --> 00:05:23.879
because you had various things
coming out of the weeds.

00:05:23.879 --> 00:05:27.045
2018, investigation has started

00:05:27.045 --> 00:05:32.045
and we become aware of
matters in terms of conflicts,

00:05:32.545 --> 00:05:37.545
actions by certain individuals
that caused some concern

00:05:38.587 --> 00:05:42.212
because things might not
quite be what they seem.

00:05:44.462 --> 00:05:46.837
So in our story we
really took a close look

00:05:46.837 --> 00:05:50.962
at Hari Nada and his role
in Carlos Ghosn's downfall.

00:05:51.879 --> 00:05:53.420
Hari Nada is one of the most

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:56.879
fascinating figures inside Nissan.

00:05:56.879 --> 00:05:58.879
He's also a lawyer.

00:05:58.879 --> 00:06:00.504
He's originally Malaysian.

00:06:00.504 --> 00:06:02.045
Hello, Mr. Hari.

00:06:02.045 --> 00:06:06.087
And he had a meteoric
rise through the company

00:06:06.087 --> 00:06:08.254
and became very, very close

00:06:08.254 --> 00:06:12.045
to Carlos Ghosn and other top figures.

00:06:12.045 --> 00:06:14.712
He had a front row seat at all

00:06:14.712 --> 00:06:18.795
the major strategic
deliberations at the company.

00:06:18.795 --> 00:06:22.045
And when he discovered that Carlos Ghosn,

00:06:22.045 --> 00:06:24.545
as his final legacy play,

00:06:24.545 --> 00:06:26.795
was going to tighten the relationship

00:06:26.795 --> 00:06:29.420
between Renault and Nissan,

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:33.587
he made a decision to
go against Carlos Ghosn.

00:06:33.587 --> 00:06:37.629
And he became one of the key figures

00:06:37.629 --> 00:06:40.420
that decided that Carlos Ghosn had to go.

00:06:47.087 --> 00:06:48.795
Hari Nada was somebody who actually

00:06:48.795 --> 00:06:50.295
recruited me into the company.

00:06:50.295 --> 00:06:54.587
So I have a long-standing
relationship with him,

00:06:54.587 --> 00:06:58.045
or did have a long-standing
relationship with him,

00:06:58.045 --> 00:06:59.920
for many, many years

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.420
he was a mentor.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.712
I had doubts about the credibility

00:07:06.712 --> 00:07:10.170
of the process right at the start.

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:15.170
Hari Nada had a plea deal
with the Tokyo prosecutors.

00:07:15.629 --> 00:07:19.837
Now that suggests he was
intrinsically involved

00:07:19.837 --> 00:07:23.420
in some of the wrongdoing, or
the allegations of wrongdoing.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:28.212
And it just didn't smell
right, just doesn't sit right.

00:07:28.212 --> 00:07:30.712
So there was a basic conflict of interest.

00:07:30.712 --> 00:07:35.712
In other words, Hari Nada
had to deliver results

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:40.712
to Japanese prosecutors to avoid
his own criminal liability,

00:07:40.712 --> 00:07:43.087
and he's accusing and leading

00:07:43.087 --> 00:07:45.879
the investigation of Carlos Ghosn.

00:07:45.879 --> 00:07:48.462
Some of the people who had been involved

00:07:48.462 --> 00:07:51.254
in the original alleged crimes

00:07:51.254 --> 00:07:54.754
were also looking into
the affairs themselves.

00:07:54.754 --> 00:07:57.337
Ravinder Passi began pointing out

00:07:57.337 --> 00:07:59.462
some of these conflict of interest issues.

00:07:59.462 --> 00:08:02.254
And the reason for that is essentially

00:08:03.462 --> 00:08:05.920
his concern was for the company.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.379
If the company's own
investigation into itself

00:08:08.379 --> 00:08:11.004
was compromised, that could lead

00:08:11.004 --> 00:08:14.712
to a very weak position
in various lawsuits

00:08:14.712 --> 00:08:17.170
that it was dealing with across the world.

00:08:19.337 --> 00:08:21.712
I had discussions with Hari,

00:08:21.712 --> 00:08:25.170
discussions with the statutory auditors

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:28.962
about these conflicts, discussions with HR

00:08:28.962 --> 00:08:30.170
about some of these conflicts,

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:34.254
because at that point
we reported into him.

00:08:34.254 --> 00:08:37.337
You know at the time everything was quite,

00:08:37.337 --> 00:08:39.295
as you can imagine, it
was, we've got to do this,

00:08:39.295 --> 00:08:41.545
we've got to do that,
we've got to move fast.

00:08:42.462 --> 00:08:44.795
But when you step back and
look at some of these things

00:08:44.795 --> 00:08:48.837
you just think, "Oh my God,
what was going on here?"

00:08:48.837 --> 00:08:53.212
Because me, members of my team

00:08:53.212 --> 00:08:57.754
were being placed in immediate danger.

00:09:00.004 --> 00:09:02.879
Your chairman's been arrested,

00:09:02.879 --> 00:09:05.670
a representative director's been arrested.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.170
They both happened to be foreigners.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:09.795
And then now what we need to do,

00:09:09.795 --> 00:09:11.004
we're being instructed to do,

00:09:11.004 --> 00:09:13.587
is certain compliance professionals

00:09:13.587 --> 00:09:16.462
need to go into properties in Brazil,

00:09:16.462 --> 00:09:19.504
for example, and retrieve evidence.

00:09:19.504 --> 00:09:20.920
They've got to do it very carefully,

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.754
because if they don't do it carefully

00:09:22.754 --> 00:09:26.545
they're going to get convicted
of criminal activities.

00:09:26.545 --> 00:09:29.837
And likewise, when a team of lawyers

00:09:29.837 --> 00:09:31.754
were commissioned to go to Lebanon,

00:09:31.754 --> 00:09:34.170
I mean, one of my immediate concerns was,

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:37.087
why are lawyers from Nissan being sent

00:09:37.087 --> 00:09:40.504
to go to Lebanon to retrieve evidence?

00:09:40.504 --> 00:09:41.629
These are just lawyers,

00:09:41.629 --> 00:09:43.545
they're corporate lawyers from Nissan.

00:09:47.129 --> 00:09:50.879
You had revelations that
a number of executives

00:09:52.045 --> 00:09:56.504
had benefited from share
appreciation rights

00:09:56.504 --> 00:09:57.587
when they shouldn't have.

00:09:57.587 --> 00:10:01.379
I mean, you know,
substantive amounts of money

00:10:01.379 --> 00:10:03.379
being taken by these guys

00:10:03.379 --> 00:10:05.754
when they weren't entitled to take them.

00:10:05.754 --> 00:10:10.379
And you do think, yes, how is
this going to look later on?

00:10:10.379 --> 00:10:12.587
It's going to look quite concerning.

00:10:15.545 --> 00:10:20.545
So that triggered for me the
sort of assessment that well,

00:10:20.962 --> 00:10:22.795
I'm going to have to do something.

00:10:22.795 --> 00:10:27.795
Because up until this point
I haven't put down on paper

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:31.629
these conflicts and these issues.

00:10:34.504 --> 00:10:37.462
So Rav Passi makes a fateful move.

00:10:37.462 --> 00:10:39.337
He writes this letter to the board

00:10:39.337 --> 00:10:44.337
listing every suspicion
he has in great detail,

00:10:44.337 --> 00:10:47.212
backed up by evidence, backed up by memos,

00:10:47.212 --> 00:10:51.712
of why this internal investigation
had serious problems.

00:10:51.712 --> 00:10:54.129
He sends the letter to the
board, and it's crickets.

00:10:54.129 --> 00:10:56.087
He doesn't hear much of anything.

00:10:56.087 --> 00:10:59.129
Nothing happened
thereafter, nothing at all.

00:10:59.129 --> 00:11:01.545
Just like it just gone into a black box.

00:11:01.545 --> 00:11:05.170
And he began to suspect
that there was a desire

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:07.879
even at the highest level within Nissan

00:11:07.879 --> 00:11:12.045
to kind of sweep these conflicts
of interest under the rug.

00:11:12.045 --> 00:11:17.045
Unfortunately for me, I
think, again with hindsight,

00:11:17.837 --> 00:11:20.420
people must've thought
that this is the nail

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:22.879
that's sticking out
and we can't have this.

00:11:26.629 --> 00:11:29.045
Within three days of me submitting that

00:11:29.045 --> 00:11:31.087
to the board of directors,

00:11:31.087 --> 00:11:33.587
that letter to the independent
board of directors,

00:11:33.587 --> 00:11:38.587
I was removed from the Ghosn
executive conduct matters.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.462
I was then told that I could not

00:11:41.462 --> 00:11:43.795
attend board meetings anymore.

00:11:43.795 --> 00:11:45.670
And up until that point

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.754
I had attended every single board meeting.

00:11:48.795 --> 00:11:50.920
I was then also told
that after eight years

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:54.962
of being in Japan, I'd
be going back to the U.----K.

00:11:55.962 --> 00:11:58.129
It eventually transpired that I'd be

00:11:58.129 --> 00:12:00.420
the VP of projects and transformation,

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:02.420
managing a team of three.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:06.004
So you can imagine what this
feels like at this stage,

00:12:07.754 --> 00:12:11.379
almost an arbitrary removal from Japan

00:12:11.379 --> 00:12:14.379
where I've lived for eight
years, had three children there,

00:12:14.379 --> 00:12:17.837
my family has grown up, and
we've been settled there,

00:12:17.837 --> 00:12:20.670
having a few months earlier been promoted

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.379
to vice president at the global level

00:12:23.379 --> 00:12:27.212
to being almost demoted.

00:12:28.129 --> 00:12:31.545
So Passi was essentially being reassigned

00:12:31.545 --> 00:12:33.379
to get him as far away

00:12:33.379 --> 00:12:36.920
from the internal
investigation as possible,

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.920
and also to a certain
extent in retaliation

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:44.420
to some of the issues that
he brought up regarding

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:47.754
the internal investigation and Hari Nada.

00:12:47.754 --> 00:12:50.879
What happened to Rav Passi can be seen

00:12:50.879 --> 00:12:53.920
as a series of corporate humiliations.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:57.129
I mean, first of all, his
immediate responsibilities

00:12:57.129 --> 00:12:58.295
were taken away from him.

00:12:58.295 --> 00:13:03.004
Eventually he'd lost the
coveted general counsel title.

00:13:03.004 --> 00:13:04.254
But it didn't stop there.

00:13:04.254 --> 00:13:07.170
Toward the end of his stay in Japan,

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:08.920
Rav and his wife were convinced

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.504
that they were being followed.

00:13:13.462 --> 00:13:18.462
During that period I'd noticed
that whilst driving my car

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:22.170
I'd have other cars following me.

00:13:24.587 --> 00:13:28.712
First time I noticed this
was at around mid-March,

00:13:28.712 --> 00:13:31.379
and I was driving, I can't
remember where I was going,

00:13:31.379 --> 00:13:33.712
but this gray van, small van

00:13:33.712 --> 00:13:35.879
just literally started following me.

00:13:36.879 --> 00:13:37.879
And I noticed that there was somebody

00:13:37.879 --> 00:13:39.462
in the car taking pictures.

00:13:41.087 --> 00:13:45.379
And lo and behold, we were
absolutely being followed

00:13:46.962 --> 00:13:51.379
either by people on foot
or other individuals,

00:13:51.379 --> 00:13:55.295
two or three, normally
two, burly men in a car,

00:13:55.295 --> 00:13:58.587
different cars at different
times, following us around.

00:13:58.587 --> 00:14:00.670
They were following the family as well.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:05.254
And, you know, given we'd seen,

00:14:06.545 --> 00:14:09.170
or I'd seen the Nissan security department

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:12.420
behave in a very, very
egregious manner with others

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:17.212
in terms of following and surveilling,

00:14:17.212 --> 00:14:19.087
I was very concerned as
to what they were doing

00:14:19.087 --> 00:14:22.629
and who they were giving
this information to.

00:14:22.629 --> 00:14:24.837
Because if they're giving this information

00:14:24.837 --> 00:14:28.295
to the authorities, you do think, why?

00:14:29.337 --> 00:14:30.629
What's going on here?

00:14:30.629 --> 00:14:34.420
I mean, this is just not normal behavior.

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.920
And this all culminated

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:41.712
in a rather dramatic event
in the middle of 2020.

00:14:41.712 --> 00:14:42.962
Who are you people?

00:14:42.962 --> 00:14:47.962
Where Nissan had hired a legal team

00:14:48.962 --> 00:14:52.337
and had obtained an unusual court order

00:14:52.337 --> 00:14:54.295
from the district court in Yokohama.

00:14:54.295 --> 00:14:59.295
To basically do a search of his home

00:15:00.045 --> 00:15:04.712
and seizure of his, you know,
corporate laptop and phone,

00:15:04.712 --> 00:15:06.879
and other document.

00:15:06.879 --> 00:15:09.254
- If you don't let us in now,

00:15:09.254 --> 00:15:11.754
we have to break this key.

00:15:11.754 --> 00:15:14.879
So it was a pretty extreme
way to treat someone

00:15:14.879 --> 00:15:17.420
who had spent 16 years at the company.

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:19.004
There's someone else at our door.

00:15:19.004 --> 00:15:20.254
These people have all come in.

00:15:20.254 --> 00:15:22.337
We don't really know who they are

00:15:22.337 --> 00:15:24.629
apart from the fact that
I've been shown a badge

00:15:24.629 --> 00:15:26.212
that says the Yokohama Court,

00:15:27.295 --> 00:15:31.879
and they're here to recover a
laptop and the mobile phone.

00:15:33.379 --> 00:15:35.629
It was even more weird

00:15:35.629 --> 00:15:38.754
because I'd highlighted to the directors

00:15:38.754 --> 00:15:43.045
that certain Nissan executives
were trying to recover

00:15:43.045 --> 00:15:46.004
this laptop and this phone
whilst I was still in Japan.

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:51.504
And I was very concerned
because it had evidence on there

00:15:51.504 --> 00:15:54.254
that related to misconduct matters

00:15:54.254 --> 00:15:58.129
and other forms of inappropriate conduct.

00:15:58.129 --> 00:16:00.920
It was just an another
form of intimidation,

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.045
another form of harassment

00:16:04.254 --> 00:16:08.337
forcing me almost to leave
the company and the country.

00:16:09.837 --> 00:16:13.754
Because once they'd retained
and obtained these items,

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:17.212
we were still followed.

00:16:17.212 --> 00:16:19.754
Which again, I just couldn't understand.

00:16:19.754 --> 00:16:22.545
What is the point of doing that?

00:16:22.545 --> 00:16:24.670
You know, this is a car company.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:25.920
This is not the KGB.

00:16:32.379 --> 00:16:34.254
I think it's fair to say that Rav Passi

00:16:34.254 --> 00:16:37.295
didn't have full battlefield awareness

00:16:37.295 --> 00:16:40.962
of all the intrigue going on at Nissan.

00:16:40.962 --> 00:16:42.504
I mean, Hari Nada is interesting

00:16:42.504 --> 00:16:45.504
because he's both
charismatic and charming,

00:16:45.504 --> 00:16:48.129
and one of the most brutal
corporate in-fighters

00:16:48.129 --> 00:16:49.629
one could ever run across.

00:16:49.629 --> 00:16:51.545
This a confidential company email, right?

00:16:51.545 --> 00:16:52.795
You should not have this.

00:16:54.212 --> 00:16:56.170
If he had fallen into line,

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:59.629
he would probably still
have his job at Nissan,

00:16:59.629 --> 00:17:03.795
be paid very well, and continued his work.

00:17:03.795 --> 00:17:08.587
A career that he spent 16
years building at Nissan

00:17:08.587 --> 00:17:10.504
is irretrievably broken.

00:17:10.504 --> 00:17:12.337
It's been smashed to smithereens.

00:17:14.545 --> 00:17:18.504
He and his family paid
a huge price, certainly.

00:17:18.504 --> 00:17:20.587
But in terms of being
able to sleep at night,

00:17:20.587 --> 00:17:23.754
I think he's come out ahead.

00:17:23.754 --> 00:17:28.754
I highlighted issues to the
highest levels of the company

00:17:29.045 --> 00:17:31.337
so that they could be
dealt with appropriately

00:17:31.337 --> 00:17:32.920
by those in charge.

00:17:33.879 --> 00:17:35.879
There was no response to those.

00:17:35.879 --> 00:17:38.295
And there was retaliation against me.

00:17:39.587 --> 00:17:43.295
What's really profound,
absolutely profound,

00:17:44.254 --> 00:17:48.129
is that none of your colleagues, I mean,

00:17:48.129 --> 00:17:52.254
people you have known
for years, forget it.

00:17:52.254 --> 00:17:53.795
Yeah.
You're on your own.

00:17:53.795 --> 00:17:54.629
Yeah.

00:17:54.629 --> 00:17:57.462
And yeah, you gotta be ready for that.

00:17:58.879 --> 00:18:00.462
You've gotta be ready for that.

00:18:02.254 --> 00:18:03.504
If you take it on anyway.

